    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0310" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg214"/>

                <head>No. 174.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Case to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy
                                Department</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-10-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 29, 1872</date>. (Received
                        October 30.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 26th instant, and to inform you that instructions have
                    been sent to Commander Byron Wilson, commanding the United States steamer
                    Yantic, to co-operate with the agent of Her Britannic Majesty’s government, in
                    any proper way, to secure the success of his mission to Muscat or Zanzibar.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. LUDLOW CASE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of the
                            Navy.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
